examples.question_text:
The mass of a substance is modelled by $m=640(0.5)^t$, where $m$ is in grams and $t$ is time in years. Its graph is shown.
(a) Read the initial mass and the mass after 2 years from the graph.
(b) State the percentage decrease each year.
(c) Explain what the horizontal asymptote $m=0$ means in this context.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{modelblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=4.4,ymin=0,ymax=700,xtick={0,1,2,3,4},ytick={0,160,320,480,640},grid=major,grid style={gridgrey},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$t$ (years)},ylabel={$m$ (g)},clip=true]
\addplot[color=modelblue,thick,domain=0:4.2,samples=100] {640*exp(x*ln(0.5))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
(a) The curve meets the vertical axis at 640 g, so the initial mass is 640 g. Reading up from $t=2$ gives approximately 160 g.

(b) $0.5=1-0.5$, so the mass decreases by $50\%$ each year.

(c) The mass approaches zero as time increases, but the model never predicts exactly zero mass. Each multiplication by 0.5 leaves a positive amount.

The dashed guides show the reading at 2 years.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{modelblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=4.4,ymin=0,ymax=700,xtick={0,1,2,3,4},ytick={0,160,320,480,640},grid=major,grid style={gridgrey},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$t$ (years)},ylabel={$m$ (g)},clip=true]
\addplot[color=modelblue,thick,domain=0:4.2,samples=100] {640*exp(x*ln(0.5))};
\addplot[black,dashed] coordinates {(2,0) (2,160) (0,160)};
\addplot[black,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(0,640) (2,160)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
